      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved with minor suggestions** — See inline comments for optional improvements.\n\n### Review Summary\n*   **Functionality:** Looks good.\n*   **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:** The new tests integrate seamlessly with the Zephyr test framework using standard `ztest` scenarios.\n*   **Code Simplicity:** Test logic is simple and straightforward.\n*   **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:** Excellent readability. Left a minor suggestion for improving the clarity of hex expected values.\n*   **Security:** N/A (test additions).\n*   **Testing:** Thorough boundary value checks and coverage of reset behaviors. Left minor suggestions for combining flags and explicitly validating the chip revision cache behavior.\n*   **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** Size: M (+110, -0). The CL focuses entirely on adding a cohesive suite of tests for the `cros_system_rtkfp` driver (Single Logical Change).\n*   **Commit Message:** The commit message correctly uses the required Chromium tags (`BUG\u003db:...`, `TEST\u003d...`) and concisely summarizes the added test scope.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/13fe2bc2-88fb-4b8c-a804-36c181a0a3d6)",
