      "message": "Since the input chip version is provided in hexadecimal (e.g., `0x00420000`, `0x00ff0000`), using hex literals for the expected return values makes the correspondence much clearer and more consistent with the final assertion (`0x34`).\n\n```c\n\tzassert_equal(cros_system_rtkfp_get_chip_version(0x00000000), 0);\n\tzassert_equal(cros_system_rtkfp_get_chip_version(0x00420000), 0x42);\n\tzassert_equal(cros_system_rtkfp_get_chip_version(0x00ff0000), 0xff);\n```\n [🔗](http://go/tj/13fe2bc2-88fb-4b8c-a804-36c181a0a3d6)",
